  "summary": "Showcasing bold coastal flavors, this seafood-forward <b>roasted Korean squid</b> delivers a perfect balance of smoky heat, mild sweetness, and tender texture. Tender whole <b>squid bodies</b> are scored with precise crosshatch cuts, allowing a fiery gochujang and sesame glaze to penetrate deep into the seafood while creating dramatic, caramelized edges as it roasts in a sizzling high-heat oven. The rapid roasting technique ensures the squid remains succulent and tender without becoming tough or chewy. Blended with garlic, soy sauce, and a touch of honey, the red pepper glaze coats every crevice of the seafood with vibrant umami complexity. Garnish the piping hot platter with fresh <b>green onions</b> and nutty toasted sesame seeds for eye-catching color and fresh crunch. Served alongside warm rice, kimchi, and pickled radish, this striking seafood roast brings authentic Korean seaside tavern flavors directly to your home kitchen in less than twenty minutes total preparation time.",
